{
 "regions": [
  {
   "id": "r2",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "65. O my mind sweep off infatuation, acquire that de-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "votion to the moon-crested god ( which grants the highest",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "bliss ); and attach thyself to the spot on the banks of the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "celestial stream; what faith ( can be placed ) in waves, bub-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "bles, streaks of lightning, women, the tips of flames, ser-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "pents, and in the currents of rivers ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "66. Do not even for once, O mind think fervidly of this",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "unstable goddess of wealth who is like a harlot sporting in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "the house like eyebrows of kings; (for now) entering through",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "the gates of houses in Benares, clad in a wallet, we await in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "the line of its streets for alms dropped into the palm of our",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "hand serving us as a pot.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "67. O mind, be hankering after the enjoyment of worldly",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "pleasures if so it is with you--if you have in front of you",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "singing, at your elbow, sentimental poets of the South, and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "behind the sportive tinkling of the bracelets of the maids in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "attendance holding chauries in their hands; otherwise, enter",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "at once upon the contemplation of Brahman.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "68. What, if wealth capable of granting all desires is",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "obtained ? What if the foot is placed on the heads of the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "enemies ? What, if we honoured supplicants ( or friends )",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "with riches ? What if the bodies of mortals have stood ( i. e.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "lasted ) for a Kalpa.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "69. If there is devotion to S'iva and the fear of ( ever-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "join"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "recurring ) death and birth present to the mind, if there",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "is no attachment to relatives and no perturbations ( of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "mind ) caused by the God of Love, if there is a forest",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "uninhabited and free from the fault of contact, and indif-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "ference towards worldly life, what else is to be desired ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "70. Therefore contemplate that Brahman which is endless,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "undecaying, sublime and pervading; what is the use of these",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "wrong notions ? Sovereignty and other pleasures, approved",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "of by mean people, follow in the train of Brahman.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
